# Frontend Components

- Keep components cleanly segregated — one component owns one concern (a page, or one self-contained piece of UI). Don't let unrelated logic accumulate in a component just because it's convenient to bolt on.
- Target **~200 lines per component**. Going over is fine when a component genuinely needs it — treat 200 as the point where you ask "should this split?", not a hard limit to engineer around.
- Split by responsibility, not just to hit a line count:
  - Extract a subcomponent when a piece of JSX has its own clear purpose.
  - Extract a hook when logic (data fetching, derived state) is reusable, or is cluttering the component body.
- Co-locate a component with the hooks/helpers only it uses. Promote something to `src/components/` (shared) or a shared hooks location only once a second component actually needs it.
